  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Born John Christopher Depp II in Owensboro, Kentucky, he left school to pursue music and moved to Los Angeles with his band. Acting followed after an introduction to an agent, and the television series 21 Jump Street made him widely known. He then chose idiosyncratic film roles, beginning a long collaboration with Tim Burton through Edward Scissorhands and later playing Ed Wood, Ichabod Crane and Sweeney Todd.\n\nDepp’s portrayal of Captain Jack Sparrow turned Pirates of the Caribbean into a global franchise and brought the first of three Academy Award nominations. He won a Golden Globe for Sweeney Todd and also produced films through Infinitum Nihil. Alongside cinema, he continued recording and performing as a guitarist, including with the rock group Hollywood Vampires, preserving the musical vocation that preceded his screen career.",
    "html": "<p>Born John Christopher Depp II in Owensboro, Kentucky, he left school to pursue music and moved to Los Angeles with his band. Acting followed after an introduction to an agent, and the television series 21 Jump Street made him widely known. He then chose idiosyncratic film roles, beginning a long collaboration with Tim Burton through Edward Scissorhands and later playing Ed Wood, Ichabod Crane and Sweeney Todd.</p>\r\n<p>Depp’s portrayal of Captain Jack Sparrow turned Pirates of the Caribbean into a global franchise and brought the first of three Academy Award nominations. He won a Golden Globe for Sweeney Todd and also produced films through Infinitum Nihil. Alongside cinema, he continued recording and performing as a guitarist, including with the rock group Hollywood Vampires, preserving the musical vocation that preceded his screen career.</p>\r\n",
